# Static part of the .graphifyignore the call graph job (pipeline/code/callgraph.ts, D67) writes into the snapshot
# checkout before every run. The job puts the scope in front of it: ignore everything, then re-include the W1 app
# folders of config/versions.json `code.<source>.w1` and, when `callgraph.apps` is true, the `apps` glob
# (src/Apps/W1/*/app). Country layers and country apps stay out: their objects share W1's ids.
# gitignore syntax, last match wins; graphify merges it after the checkout's own .gitignore.
#
# Below: files graphify would extract that are not AL. The documents, media and office files are the bc-code-atlas
# template (build/build/graphify.ignore.template); the code extensions are the ones BCApps ships next to its AL
# (app.json and permission JSON, control add-in scripts, build scripts). Changing this file changes the graph key:
# every snapshot major runs `linked` again.
*.md
*.mdx
*.qmd
*.txt
*.rst
*.html
*.yaml
*.yml
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.svg
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.mkv
*.avi
*.m4v
*.mp3
*.wav
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.json
*.js
*.mjs
*.cjs
*.ts
*.tsx
*.jsx
*.css
*.ps1
*.psm1
*.psd1
*.cs
*.csproj
*.sln
*.sql
*.sh
*.py
*.xaml
